			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1490,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Enable telemetry collection defaults and enforce consent gates\n\nReverse the default build-time values for PostHog (`Report`), OTLP (`OTLPEnabled`), and trace capture (`Capture`) from 'false' to 'true' in `build.rs`. This enables telemetry by default for the current development cycle, allowing the team to collect diagnostic data unless explicitly disabled via environment variables.\n\nSimultaneously, reinforce runtime safety in `scripts/cocoon/bootstrap-fork.js` by adding explicit environment variable checks before any network request. The `PostHogCapture` and `OTLPFlush` functions now verify that `Report`, `Capture`, and `OTLPEnabled` are strictly set to 'true' before proceeding. This ensures that even with production builds enabled in the build script, no data is sent without explicit runtime consent, maintaining the privacy barrier for production environments while facilitating data collection during development.\n\nThis change aligns the build defaults with the telemetry requirements for the current `Current` branch while preserving the logical gatekeeping in the Extension Host sidecar.",
			"SHA": "dfe7c6e4e60e8d589ce3eccb516e905a78c45cee"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-13T17:23:42Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1490,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Mountain): Disable telemetry collection by default in build script\n\nUpdate the default values in build.rs for telemetry-related environment variables (`Report`, `OTLPEnabled`, `Capture`). Change the defaults from \"true\" to \"false\" to ensure no telemetry data is captured or sent unless explicitly enabled via environment configuration.\n\nThis aligns the default build behavior with privacy best practices for development and distribution, requiring an explicit opt-in for PostHog, OTLP, and trace capture mechanisms.",
			"SHA": "9cdc391367fd3acde2f55bdac84728cbe413d47a"
		}
